{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"evidence\":[{\"source\":\"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 天津古籍出版社、遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692; attached source scan directly inspected\",\"field\":\"好 headword, formation and meaning discussion; printed p. 1094 / PDF p. 1109\",\"text\":\"The scan shows the actual 好 entry. It identifies oracle-bone, bronze, Warring States and Shuowen seal forms as 女 plus 子, and the author calls its original meaning ‘woman’, then describes extension to beauty/goodness and a verbal ‘like/love’ sense. The page cites Shang personal name 婦好 and 《合集》6412. This is the book author’s account, not independent proof of the proposed original sense or a complete semantic chronology. I visually checked the word introducing the bronze example: the scan reads 虘鐘, not the provisional OCR 虐钟. Proposed source-bound OCR correction only; no corpus correction made.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"book_scan_inspected\",\"url\":\"https://books.google.com/books/about/%E5%AD%97%E6%BA%90.html?id=xqP9zAEACAAJ\",\"title\":\"《字源》, 2012 edition — bibliographic record\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"《字源》, 李學勤主編, 天津古籍出版社、遼寧人民出版社, 2012, ISBN 9787552800692; attached source scan directly inspected\",\"field\":\"好 verbal-sense continuation; printed p. 1095 / PDF p. 1110 (continuation passage supplied as OCR locator; page scan not attached in this invocation)\",\"text\":\"The supplied continuation OCR states that 好 read hào means ‘like/love’ and cites the Analects. I did not inspect PDF page 1110 pixels in this invocation, so treat this as a locator lead, not scan-verified evidence. The attached p. 1094 image itself ends with the sentence continuing onto the next page.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"book_scan_partial\",\"url\":\"https://books.google.com/books/about/%E5%AD%97%E6%BA%90.html?id=xqP9zAEACAAJ\",\"title\":\"《字源》, 2012 edition — bibliographic record\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"CUHK Humanum, 漢語多功能字庫\",\"field\":\"形義通解; Shuowen and Guangyun readings; dated use reports\",\"text\":\"The entry analyzes ordinary 好 as 女 plus 子 and lists proposed original motivations: woman’s beauty (Duan Yucai), mother–child affection (Liu Shengyou), and man–woman affection (Xu Kai and Chen Weizhan). Its editor favors the mother–child account partly because early 子 forms depict a child and are smaller than 女, while explicitly noting that cited early uses do not attest that proposed sense. The entry separately reports 好 in 婦好 as possibly 女 with phonetic 子, read 子 and representing the Shang 子 lineage name. It reports bronze examples for ‘good/beautiful’, ‘friendly’, and a loan use for 孝, and Warring States bamboo examples for ‘like’ and friendly relations. The listed examples do not establish a full semantic chain or an absolute date for the cited bronze vessels. Shuowen is recorded as 美也，从女、子; Guangyun fanqie 呼晧 and 呼到 occur in distinct tone categories.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"dictionary_entry\",\"url\":\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/search.php?word=%E5%A5%BD\",\"title\":\"漢語多功能字庫 — 好\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Taiwan Ministry of Education, Dictionary of Chinese Character Variants\",\"field\":\"說文釋形; modern readings and senses\",\"text\":\"The official entry records the transmitted Shuowen analysis 从女、子 and both Mandarin readings hǎo and hào. It documents current senses including beautiful, good, friendly, intact, recovered, degree ‘very’, completion, ease, purpose and favorability before verbs; hào includes ‘love/like’. This lexical list records meanings and examples, not a dated semantic development.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"dictionary_entry\",\"url\":\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A00883\",\"title\":\"[A00883] 好 — 教育部《異體字字典》\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Academia Sinica, Institute of History and Philology, Character Database\",\"field\":\"好 graphic evolution and interpretive alternatives\",\"text\":\"The record indexes oracle-bone example 合集154, bronze example 集成00088, and a Shuowen form. It summarizes interpretations of 女 plus 子 as either a woman holding a child/new birth or a beautiful woman. The text corroborates that these interpretations are in circulation, but the database glyph images were not visually inspected and the record does not resolve the original motivation.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"database_entry\",\"url\":\"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=9605\",\"title\":\"漢字「好」：字形演變\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"University of Michigan, Baxter–Sagart Old Chinese reconstruction v1.1\",\"field\":\"好 / paired lexical readings\",\"text\":\"The table lists Mandarin hǎo ‘good’ as Middle Chinese xawX and Old Chinese *qʰˤuʔ, and hào ‘love, like (verb)’ as xawH and *qʰˤuʔ-s. These are reconstructed readings of the whole character in two lexical uses. The 女-plus-子 ordinary graph analysis does not propose either component as phonetic.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"phonology_data\",\"url\":\"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\"title\":\"Baxter-Sagart Old Chinese reconstruction, version 1.1\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"},{\"source\":\"Local primary reading extract, pipeline/data/unihan-kmandarin-hsk1.tsv; exact local rows supplied in task input\",\"field\":\"kMandarin rows for 好, 女 and 子; corresponding official Unicode Unihan records attempted\",\"text\":\"The supplied local rows give 好 hǎo, 女 nǚ, and 子 zǐ. Unicode's character-specific GetUnihanData URLs were attempted but returned internal errors in the browser; the Unicode site documentation describes Unihan data and kMandarin, but these failed character pages are not cited as successfully inspected character evidence. These current readings do not establish an ancient sound relationship; no phonetic role is proposed for the ordinary 好 components.\",\"record_character\":\"好\",\"kind\":\"local_reading_with_upstream_access_gap\",\"url\":\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=597D\",\"title\":\"Unicode Unihan record for 好 — lookup failed\",\"accessed_at\":\"2026-10-03\"}],\"search_audit\":[{\"query\":\"好 漢語多功能字庫 形義通解 母子 情愛 婦好; 好 字源 甲骨文 金文 本義 女子 虘鐘 用樂好賓; 教育部 異體字字典 好 甲骨文 女 子 字形\",\"urls\":[\"https://humanum.arts.cuhk.edu.hk/Lexis/lexi-mf/search.php?word=%E5%A5%BD\",\"https://dict.variants.moe.edu.tw/dictView.jsp?educode=A00883\",\"https://chardb.iis.sinica.edu.tw/evolution.jsp?cid=9605\"],\"outcome\":\"Search found the CUHK Humanum entry, Taiwan MOE variants dictionary and Academia Sinica character database. Opened all three; inspected the CUHK text on competing formation accounts, reported examples and phonological data, the MOE entry, and the Sinica text summary. Sinica glyph images were not inspected.\"},{\"query\":\"site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=597D 好 kMandarin; site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5973 女 kMandarin; site:unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5B50 子 kMandarin\",\"urls\":[\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=597D\",\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5973\",\"https://www.unicode.org/cgi-bin/GetUnihanData.pl?codepoint=5B50\"],\"outcome\":\"Search did not return character-specific kMandarin records. Open attempts for each official Unicode record returned internal errors; they are recorded as access failures, not inspected evidence.\"},{\"query\":\"University Michigan Baxter Sagart 好 qʰˤuʔ *qʰˤuʔ-s pdf; site:unicode.org/Public/UCD/latest/ucd/Unihan.zip Unihan_Readings.txt\",\"urls\":[\"https://ocbaxtersagart.lsait.lsa.umich.edu/BaxterSagartOCbyRadStr2014-09-20.pdf\",\"https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr38/\",\"https://www.unicode.org/Public/UNIDATA/\"],\"outcome\":\"Opened the Baxter–Sagart table result and checked its paired 好 readings. Unicode documentation confirms Unihan.zip contains Unihan_Readings.txt and the official public index exposes the archive; character-specific Unihan rows remained inaccessible in this browser.\"}],\"gaps\":[\"[OCR CORRECTION REQUIRED] 《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, printed p. 1094 / PDF p. 1109: provisional corpus OCR span 虐钟 in the bronze-example phrase should be checked for producer correction to scan-visible 虘鐘. The attached full-page pixels show the rare vessel-name graph as 虘 followed by 鐘; this report proposes the literal correction but did not alter the corpus.\",\"[SCAN VERIFICATION REQUIRED] 《字源》, 李學勤主編, 2012, printed p. 1095 / PDF p. 1110: continuation sentence beginning “好”读为 hào was available only as supplied OCR in this invocation; its source scan pixels were not attached or opened here. Check that page and the continuation before treating this passage as scan-verified.\",\"The original motivation of ordinary 好 remains unresolved: the consulted accounts preserve mother–child affection, woman’s beauty, and man–woman affection proposals. CUHK explicitly notes that its cited early examples do not attest mother–child affection directly.\",\"The cited sources report selected inscriptional and bamboo uses but do not establish the earliest ordinary lexical ‘good’ use, an absolute date for the bronze example, or a complete sequence connecting ‘good/beautiful’, ‘friendly’, and verbal ‘like’. Keep the Shang name 婦好 analytically separate; CUHK reports a distinct homograph/phonetic analysis for that name.\",\"The character-specific Unicode Unihan records for 好 U+597D, 女 U+5973 and 子 U+5B50 could not be opened despite direct attempts. The supplied local extract supports current kMandarin readings; upstream click-through verification remains incomplete. No phonetic comparison is needed for the ordinary 女-plus-子 semantic analysis.\",\"No independent primary inscription edition was opened for the cited 《合集》 and bronze-vessel examples. These remain reports attributed to the inspected CUHK reference and the scanned 字源 passage.\"]}"}}
